{%- comment -%}
MIM size guide page (/pages/how-to-measure, rendered by sections/mim-page.liquid).
Built on our own Find My Size model (snippets/mim-size-finder-core in page mode + assets/mim-size-finder.js):
1. Garment tabs (dress / top / pants) feed the finder's garment model; the big "Find my size" card opens the same 3-step finder.
2. Size chart drawn from the finder's own body chart (bust / waist / hips per size, same numbers the model uses), cm/in toggle,
   relaxed sizes 1–4 mapped the way the model maps them; the recommended size row lights up (event `mim:size`).
3. How to measure: 4 animated steps; tapping a step highlights the matching line on the figure.
The page body (the old measuring image) stays available in a fold at the end. No extra requests beyond the finder's own files.
{%- endcomment -%}
